# Project Structure Guide

This is a React Native/Expo mobile application called "BrainDrop" (organized-notes-mobile). The project uses Expo Router for navigation and follows a feature-based architecture.

## Key Entry Points

- [app/\_layout.tsx](mdc:app/_layout.tsx) - Root layout with Sentry integration, font loading, and toast configuration
- [app/index.tsx](mdc:app/index.tsx) - Main app entry point
- [package.json](mdc:package.json) - Project dependencies and scripts

## Core Architecture

- **App Directory**: Uses Expo Router with file-based routing in the `app/` directory
- **Source Code**: Main source code is in `src/` with the following structure:
  - `src/core/` - Shared utilities, hooks, UI components, and configurations
  - `src/features/` - Feature-based modules (category, note)
  - `src/routes/` - Route definitions and navigation logic

## UI System

The project has a comprehensive UI system in `src/core/ui/`:

- [src/core/ui/constants/Colors.ts](mdc:src/core/ui/constants/Colors.ts) - Theme colors with light/dark variants
- [src/core/ui/constants/Typography.ts](mdc:src/core/ui/constants/Typography.ts) - Typography system using Geist fonts
- [src/core/ui/base/](mdc:src/core/ui/base/) - Base UI components (Button, Text, Card, etc.)
- [src/core/ui/constants/Layout.ts](mdc:src/core/ui/constants/Layout.ts) - Layout constants and spacing

## Key Technologies

- **Expo SDK 52** with React Native 0.76.9
- **Expo Router** for navigation
- **TypeScript** with strict mode enabled
- **React Query** for data fetching
- **Sentry** for error tracking
- **React Hook Form** for form management
- **Geist Fonts** for typography

## Development Scripts

- `yarn start` - Start Expo development server
- `yarn android` / `yarn ios` - Run on specific platforms
- `yarn lint-check` - Check code quality
- `yarn lint-fix` - Fix linting issues
